exp="Sawtooth flutter waves best seen in <b>II, III and aVF</b> are <b>atrial flutter</b>. With <b>4:1 conduction</b>, four flutter waves occur for each QRS: ventricular rate 75 × 4 = <b>atrial rate 300/min</b>, the typical rate of the right atrial macro-re-entry circuit around the tricuspid annulus. Fixed 4:1 conduction makes the rhythm regular; variable conduction makes it irregular, so flutter can fall on either side of the regular-versus-irregular split. With 2:1 conduction the ventricle runs at about 150.<br><br><b>Educational objective:</b> In atrial flutter the atria fire at about 300/min; the ventricular rate is 300 ÷ the conduction ratio (150 at 2:1, 75 at 4:1).",
